  ],
  "description": "Circuit approximation of the early 15-frequency proportional-Q API 550A, distinct from the later constant-Q 550A-1. Retains editable analog Twin-T filters with linked bandwidth and reciprocal stepped gain, peak/shelf outer bands, 50 Hz–15 kHz bandpass, and transformer output. Gain magnitude is selected in 2, 4, 6, 9 and 12 dB steps, with a separate Cut toggle. The highest engaged step or frequency has precedence. The analog filter and driver cards and their switch-routing equivalent are modeled from the documented response family, with linear op-amp models in the filter stages and the API2520 card used for the output driver.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [],
    "switches": [
      "Bandpass 50 Hz–15 kHz",
      "Low Cut",
      "Low 2 dB",
      "Low 4 dB",
      "Low 6 dB",
      "Low 9 dB",
      "Low 12 dB",
      "Low 100 Hz",
      "Low 200 Hz",
      "Low 300 Hz",
      "Low 400 Hz",
